<h1 class="mb-3">Privacy Policy</h1>

<p>
    This Privacy Policy explains how VeriPay collects, uses, stores, and protects personal and
    transactional information processed through the system. VeriPay is an internal payment
    verification and fraud-monitoring platform used solely for organisational purposes.
</p>

<h3 class="mt-4">1. Information We Collect</h3>
<p>
    VeriPay processes the following categories of information:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>Employee account information (e.g., username, role, access permissions)</li>
    <li>Payment and transaction records captured by staff</li>
    <li>System-generated metadata such as audit logs, timestamps, and risk scores</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="mt-4">2. How Information Is Used</h3>
<p>
    Information processed through VeriPay is used exclusively for:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>Payment verification and audit trails</li>
    <li>Fraud detection and risk analysis</li>
    <li>Internal reporting and decision-making</li>
    <li>Security monitoring and system optimisation</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="mt-4">3. Data Protection & Security</h3>
<p>
    VeriPay implements strict controls to safeguard all information, including:
</p>
<ul>
    <li>Role-based access control (RBAC)</li>
    <li>Encrypted communication between services</li>
    <li>Secure storage of ML scoring results and audit logs</li>
    <li>Restricted access to sensitive internal data</li>
</ul>

<h3 class="mt-4">4. Machine Learning & Automated Processing</h3>
<p>
    VeriPay uses machine learning models to generate fraud-risk scores based on transaction
    patterns. These automated scores support decision-making but do not replace final human
    judgment. All flagged transactions remain subject to internal review.
</p>

<h3 class="mt-4">5. Data Sharing & Retention</h3>
<p>
    All information processed by VeriPay is used only within the organisation. No data is shared
    externally unless required for authorised audits or legal compliance. Retention periods follow
    institutional and financial governance policies.
</p>

<h3 class="mt-4">6. User Responsibilities</h3>
<p>
    Users must ensure that information entered into VeriPay is accurate and must follow all
    organisational security and confidentiality guidelines when accessing the system.
</p>

<h3 class="mt-4">7. Contact</h3>
<p>
    For privacy-related queries or concerns, please contact your system administrator or the IT
    Governance office.
</p>
